# Snapshots ARE committed on purpose.
#
# They were originally ignored as "local artefacts". That was wrong, and it cost us:
# the Phase 1 baseline was lost before Phase 2.2 could be compared against it, because
# nothing outside a working directory ever held a copy.
#
# A snapshot is the recorded expected structure of the application at a known commit.
# That is source-of-truth material, not a build artefact - it is the only thing a later
# phase can be diffed against, and it has to survive a clean checkout.
#
# Keep one snapshot per sub-phase, never overwriting: after-2.1.json, after-2.2.json, ...
# `capture` refuses to overwrite an existing file unless you pass --force.
